      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "εἰ δὲ ὑπονοίᾳ αὐτοῦ κεχράτησαι ὡς ἀληθοῦς",
          "english_quote": "But if you are held by its supposition as true",
          "issue": "The draft understandably interprets κεχράτησαι as a passive holding verb, but it does not disclose the apparent spelling irregularity relative to the regular κεκράτησαι. Its English is also unnecessarily obscure: ‘its supposition as true’ does not clearly express a supposition concerning the account’s truth. The verified supplied spelling must not be silently regularized or labeled an OCR error.",
          "suggested_revision": "Propose ‘But if you have been gripped by the supposition that it is true,’ with a source-quoted note identifying κεχράτησαι as the supplied reading and explaining the contextual passive interpretation. Identify κεκράτησαι only as a proposed regularization, not verified replacement text. Preserve the already adequate four-dot gap and its source-quoted nonrestoration note unchanged. The proposed wording and disclosure require fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
